{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1466285-rite-of-death-to-reincarnate-normal-people-as-kinfolk","id":1466285,"title":"Rite of death to reincarnate normal people as kinfolk","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-02T07:53:13-07:00","id":1466285,"title":"Rite of death to reincarnate normal people as kinfolk","content":"had this idea a while<br /> <br /> <br /> Think have to get 3 successes to properly petition the incarna<br /> <br /> one or 2 succeses causes you to come to their notice enough to be born as a gaffling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T15:08:12-07:00","id":1466342,"title":"","content":"I don't see the point. Even if it is a human you trust there's no guarantee you could trust him after the reincarnation. Besides the most common trait kinfolks have is their Delirium immunity. It's because they are garou's family. I once read that Children of Gaia found a way to &quot;adopt&quot; certain mortals by using Rending the Veil Rite on them. IMHO it's safer that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T15:19:04-07:00","id":1466345,"title":"","content":"I think you could go further than that and made a rite to turn normal people into kinfolk in this life. Doing so through reincarnation isn't really a big enough challenge to even need a rite, and if so, it would be just 1 success.<br /> <br /> What could really be a big deal would be to reincarnate normal people as Garou, especially if you rite guarantees that the new incarnation will keep memories. Reincarnating as Kinfolk may be useful if it keeps memories and happens quickly, like a rite that turns the corpse into a living baby in a matter of days at most.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T10:47:27-07:00","id":1466494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1466285-rite-of-death-to-reincarnate-normal-people-as-kinfolk?p=1466345#post1466345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you could go further than that and made a rite to turn normal people into kinfolk in this life. Doing so through reincarnation isn't really a big enough challenge to even need a rite, and if so, it would be just 1 success.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe that Rending the Veil Rite could be used that way as I wrote earlier. Mechanically I think the difficulty of the basic rite should be risen, but effectively you get some kind of quasi-kinfolk, with Delirium immunity, no gifts, rites etc (they could learn them later) and no Pure Breed (for determining the chance of giving birth to garou). I would also and notoriety flaw to both &quot;newborn&quot; kinfolk and the ritemaster, as they both would be suspicious for other Garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T19:02:29-07:00","id":1466576,"title":"","content":"A Quasi-Kinfolk isn't a Kinfolk. Even a Pure Breed 0 Kinfolk is significantly more likely than a <i>Delirium-Immune</i> normal human to pass this on to their children or to have a Garou child. They may also not be able to perform Rites.<br /> <br /> Unless you houserule Rending the Veil to make for almost Kinfolk, which is the same as making a new rite for the same or full effect. The specialized rite may also be able to create a Pure Breed rank if it have enough successes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T19:43:18-07:00","id":1466587,"title":"","content":"the idea of becoming a gaffling on a partial success is gafflings are just minions servants wheras kinfolk are family.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-15T04:48:16-08:00","id":1467866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1466285-rite-of-death-to-reincarnate-normal-people-as-kinfolk?p=1466576#post1466576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Quasi-Kinfolk isn't a Kinfolk. Even a Pure Breed 0 Kinfolk is significantly more likely than a <i>Delirium-Immune</i> normal human to pass this on to their children or to have a Garou child. They may also not be able to perform Rites.<br /> <br /> Unless you houserule Rending the Veil to make for almost Kinfolk, which is the same as making a new rite for the same or full effect. The specialized rite may also be able to create a Pure Breed rank if it have enough successes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, but IMHO it would be quasi-kinfolk only for other tribes. Children of Gaia are known for adopting the most valuable mortals. Sooner or later a mortal like that will have to be introduced into garou ways. But knowledge doesn't mean Delirium Immunity. So there's a rite. For me it is some kind of adoption.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-15T16:58:45-08:00","id":1467943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1466285-rite-of-death-to-reincarnate-normal-people-as-kinfolk?p=1467866#post1467866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, but IMHO it would be quasi-kinfolk only for other tribes. Children of Gaia are known for adopting the most valuable mortals. Sooner or later a mortal like that will have to be introduced into garou ways. But knowledge doesn't mean Delirium Immunity. So there's a rite. For me it is some kind of adoption.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's not the point.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1153\" data-vbnamecard=\"1153\">Prince of the Night</a> didn't talked about adopting humans in their midst, it was about turning humans into Kinfolk. Adoption into a tribe isn't mentioned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1466285-rite-of-death-to-reincarnate-normal-people-as-kinfolk?p=1466587#post1466587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the idea of becoming a gaffling on a partial success is gafflings are just minions servants wheras kinfolk are family.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if this would be needed. Gafflings are another thing entirely, this actually gives too much metaphysical power to the Rite just to have a lower outcome for few successes.<br /> <br /> At most I could see the Gaffling thing as the result of a botch, locking a human into an outcome that is actually &quot;worse&quot; than the normal destiny of a human soul.<br /> <br /> But even then, I don't think it is needed here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-15T17:15:25-08:00","id":1467945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1466285-rite-of-death-to-reincarnate-normal-people-as-kinfolk?p=1467943#post1467943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that's not the point.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1153\" data-vbnamecard=\"1153\">Prince of the Night</a> didn't talked about adopting humans in their midst, it was about turning humans into Kinfolk. Adoption into a tribe isn't mentioned.</div> </div> </div> </div> If you want to look that way then my answer is no, there is no such way. To be a kinfolk you have to have/had garou amongst your kin. No rite would make this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 11-15-2021, 08:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T06:47:44-08:00","id":1468128,"title":"","content":"You could create a very high level rite that can merge a spiritual wolf inside a kinfolk to turn him into a real werewolf. Or even ancestral and forgotten gift that give the werewolf the legendary ability to turn a human into a werewolf. In that case the human would be completely mind opened by the wolf instinct and his new spiritual aspect and the discovery of Ga\u00efa would push him to join the fight<br /> <br /> If you like the idea of the rite play it like that: a pack meet a human that is worthy to become a kinfolk. The pack bring him to the caern and that man or woman has to complete several tests. If he is successful the werewolves do the rite that bound that man to the spiritual world","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 11-17-2021, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T08:39:12-08:00","id":1468138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1466285-rite-of-death-to-reincarnate-normal-people-as-kinfolk?p=1468128#post1468128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In that case the human would be completely mind opened by the wolf instinct and his new spiritual aspect and the discovery of Ga\u00efa would push him to join the fight</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't like in the slightest the idea of making assumptions on how the character will react. Choosing carefully and explaining beforehand should be a part of the preparation, not something hand waved by the magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T10:33:25-08:00","id":1468152,"title":"","content":"I meant that he would be like a werewolf before his first changes, he would become uncomfortable around humans and technology, would react more negatively to the impact of humans on nature and would be attracted to, or at least comfortable in wild environments, as if he belonged there.<br /> <br /> Obviously he would not be suddenly ready to join the garou nation but it would be easier for him to learn<br /> <br /> Oh and to counterbalance that rite or gift, the werewolf should be cautious about who he is biting; a corrupted human would turn into a corrupted werewolf. As human are too comfortable with technology, the food as will etc... the potential new werewolf or kinfolk should be selected with a lot of precaution to not create a new ennemy instead of a new ally","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}